UPDATE companies SET description='Casco Bay Molding was founded in February 2000 by Andrew Powell in Sanford, Maine, with a vision for producing silicone and thermoplastic products domestically. The company’s earliest offerings included a scuba line of mouthpieces, regulator straps, and octopus necklaces.

Today the firm operates as a vertically integrated, FDA‑registered, ISO 13485:2016‑certified product development and injection molding facility. Its Sanford factory houses an in‑house machine shop that builds and maintains precision tooling, enabling silicone and thermoplastic injection molding, over‑molding, ultrasonic welding, assembly, and inspection. The company reports over two decades of production experience and has manufactured more than one million menstrual cups for global B2B customers, alongside high‑volume runs of medical device components such as CPAP parts, surgical handles, valves, and custom gaskets.

Casco Bay Molding serves primarily the medical device sector (Class I and II), supplying OEMs, startups, and NGOs with products ranging from respiratory equipment and surgical instruments to menstrual health devices like the patented Flip Disc and Wandah applicator. The company also produces components for energy extraction, scuba gear, and PPE — notably the Casco Shield face shield developed during the COVID‑19 pandemic in partnership with Thermoformers of New England.

The business was started to keep silicone and thermoplastic manufacturing in the United States. Its differentiation lies in combining design, tooling, production, and regulatory support under one roof, reducing mold lead times and costs through in‑house toolmaking. The team’s background at firms such as Nypro, Netstal, and Shape, plus automation partnerships with EAM and Province Automation, supports a vertically integrated development cycle that the company says turns clinical insights into market‑ready devices.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001 (since 2003)','FDA registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Silicone injection molding", "Thermoplastic injection molding", "Over-molding (multi-durometer)", "In-house precision tooling and mold making", "Product development and design for medical devices", "Medical device manufacturing (Class I and II)", "Ultrasonic welding", "Assembly and handling", "Inspection and quality control", "FDA product registration support", "Retail packaging", "Menstrual cup and disc manufacturing", "CPAP component manufacturing", "Face shield (PPE) manufacturing", "Scuba gear manufacturing", "Medical-grade silicone processing", "Biocompatibility assessment", "Precision machining", "Tooling design and fabrication", "Process validation", "Automation integration (with partners)", "Custom gasket manufacturing", "Medical valve and tube manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical devices (Class I and II)", "Menstrual health products", "Respiratory equipment (CPAP)", "Surgical instruments", "Energy extraction", "Scuba and diving equipment", "Personal protective equipment (PPE)", "Women''s health", "Non-governmental organizations (humanitarian aid)"], "materials": ["Medical-grade silicone", "Thermoplastics", "Polypropylene", "Silicone (various durometers)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 1 million menstrual cups; high-volume silicone and thermoplastic production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated design, tooling, production, and regulatory support under one roof", "In\u2011house precision tooling and machine shop that cuts mold lead time and cost", "ISO 13485:2016 certified and FDA registered for Class I and II medical devices", "Over one million menstrual cups produced for global B2B customers", "Patented menstrual disc designs (Flip Disc hinge and over\u2011molded durometer transition)"], "facts_used": ["Founded February 2000 by Andrew Powell in Sanford, Maine -> /about-us", "ISO 9001 certified since 2003 -> /about-us", "ISO 13485:2016 certified January 2020 -> /about-us", "FDA registered and passed FDA inspection September 2019 -> /about-us", "Vertically integrated with in-house machine shop for tooling -> /", "Specializes in high-volume silicone and thermoplastic injection molding -> /", "Over a million menstrual cups manufactured for global B2B customers -> /", "Medical device components: surgical handles, CPAP parts, valves, tubes, gaskets -> /", "Patented Flip Disc (hinge design and over-molding) -> /", "Wandah applicator developed with nurse practitioner Hope Jensen -> /", "Casco Shield face shield developed with Thermoformers of New England (2020) -> /", "Maine MEP Manufacturer of the Year 2018 -> /about-us", "Partnership with Legu Tool & Mold for in-house tooling (2016) -> /about-us", "Team experience from Nypro, Netstal, Shape, EAM, First Light Technologies -> /about-us", "Automation partners EAM and Province Automation -> /about-us", "Materials: medical-grade silicone, thermoplastics, polypropylene -> /", "Processes: injection molding, over-molding, ultrasonic welding, assembly, inspection -> /", "Industries: medical, menstrual health, respiratory, surgical, energy extraction, scuba, PPE -> /", "Headquarters: Sanford, Maine -> db", "Founded year: 2000 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Casco Bay Molding is a vertically integrated, FDA registered, ISO 13485:2016 Certified product development and injection molding facility located in Sanford, Maine.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='casco-bay-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Case Medical, Inc. was founded in 1992 in Bloomfield, New Jersey, as a supplier of custom graphics trays to medical device manufacturers. The company remains a U.S.-based manufacturer of medical instrument processing solutions.

Today the company produces DIN-sized SteriTite® universal sealed containers, modular MediTray® inserts, SuperNova® cleaning chemistries, CaseTrak360® tracking software, IFU Scanner, and SteriTite® case carts. It also offers custom instrument set assembly, validation services, and consulting through its Case Academy. No facility size or headcount is disclosed.

Customers include hospitals, surgical centers, and medical device manufacturers that operate sterile processing departments and operating rooms. The firm’s container system is FDA-cleared for all current sterilization modalities, and its chemistries are used for instrument decontamination. The company also provides OEM tracking software for medical device makers.

Case Medical differentiates itself through universal compatibility, sustainability recognition as a three-time U.S. EPA Safer Choice Partner of the Year (2022–2024), independent laboratory validation, and a patent-pending Digital Visualization feature that adds AI-driven workflow to its containers. The business began with custom trays and evolved to set what it calls the gold standard in instrument protection and organization.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical instrument processing solutions", "Sterilization container manufacturing", "Cleaning chemistry formulation", "Software development (CaseTrak360, IFU Scanner)", "Custom instrument set assembly", "Validation testing", "Consulting and education (Case Academy)", "Cost benefit analysis", "OEM tracking software for medical devices"], "industries": ["Healthcare facilities", "Medical device manufacturers", "Sterile processing departments", "Operating rooms", "Medical device reprocessing", "Infection prevention"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SteriTite sealed container", "MediTray modular inserts", "SuperNova cleaning chemistries", "CaseTrak360 software", "IFU Scanner", "SteriTite case carts"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Three-time U.S. EPA Safer Choice Partner of the Year (2022, 2023, 2024)", "FDA-cleared container system for all sterilization modalities", "Products validated by independent laboratories and universities", "Customizable instrument sets tailored to surgeon preferences", "Patent filed for Digital Visualization with AI-enhanced workflow"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> db", "Headquarters Bloomfield, New Jersey -> db", "U.S. manufacturer of medical instrument processing solutions -> /", "Started as supplier of custom graphics trays to medical device manufacturers -> /", "Products: SteriTite universal sealed container, MediTray inserts, SuperNova chemistries, CaseTrak360 software, IFU Scanner, SteriTite case carts -> /", "EPA Safer Choice Partner of the Year 2022, 2023, 2024 -> /", "FDA-cleared container system for all sterilization modalities -> /", "Validated by independent laboratories and universities -> /", "Customizable instrument sets based on surgeons'' preferences -> /", "Patent filed for Digital Visualization -> /", "Holistic 360-degree approach -> /", "Serves healthcare facilities, medical device manufacturers, sterile processing departments, operating rooms -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Case Medical, Inc. is a U.S. manufacturer of high quality, cost effective instrument processing products and services.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='case-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clark brought more than 30 years of respiratory experience and identified a service gap that larger providers were not addressing, prompting the couple to create a locally focused alternative.

The company delivers respiratory and mobility services with a staff that remains on call 24 hours a day. Operations emphasize a hometown care model where patients and team members interact on a first-name basis, and the founders describe a guiding principle of family that shapes daily interactions and service delivery.

The business serves individuals requiring respiratory support and mobility assistance in the Casper area. Its customer base consists of patients seeking personalized, community-based care rather than institutional-scale providers.

The McInroys started the venture to offer a family atmosphere and responsive service that they felt was missing from the market. They position the company around continuous availability, patient comfort, and a relational approach that contrasts with larger, less personal operators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Respiratory services", "Mobility solutions", "24/7 on-call support", "Patient education and comfort"], "industries": ["Respiratory care", "Mobility assistance"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Staff on call 24/7", "Hometown care and family atmosphere", "Patients and staff on a first-name basis", "Guiding principle: family"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2020 by Clark and Lynnette McInroy -> /", "Clark has over 30 years respiratory experience -> /", "Located in Casper, Wyoming -> db", "Staff on call 24/7 -> /", "Hometown care, family atmosphere, first-name basis -> /", "Staff names: Tamara Hopkins, Tiffany Piper, Leah Larson, Jamie Shaw -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our staff is on call 24/7 and we strive to find solutions that fit all lifestyles. Our patients come first and we believe in one guiding principle- family.", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='casper-respiratory-and-mobility-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cassling was founded in 1984 in Omaha, Nebraska, by Bob Cassling. The company transitioned to 100% employee ownership and is now led by Chairman Mike Cassling, who joined the firm in 1985 after working alongside his father, and CEO Kyle Salem, Ph.D., who joined in 2005. Headquartered in Omaha, the business operates with Midwestern values and a focus on community healthcare.

As an Advanced Partner of Siemens Healthineers, Cassling distributes and services diagnostic imaging equipment from Siemens, Hologic, and GE Healthcare surgical C-arms. The company provides equipment maintenance per OEM specifications, flexible service coverage plans, applications training, consulting, continuing education, financing, marketing, project management, and site planning for healthcare facilities. Its service team works locally across the region to keep imaging systems operational.

Cassling serves hospitals, health systems, imaging centers, ambulatory surgery centers, rural healthcare providers, Veterans Affairs facilities, and physician groups across specialties including cardiology, neurology, oncology, orthopedics, pain management, pediatrics, radiology, surgery, and women''s health. Customers include the Urology Cancer Center & GU Research Network and Methodist Jennie Edmundson Hospital.

