UPDATE companies SET description='Castillo Electric Distribution was founded in 2006 in Signal Hill, California, as an electrician-run wholesale electrical supplier. The company was established on a commitment to quality, expertise, and reliability, aiming to provide electricians and contractors with the right products at the right time.

The company distributes a full range of electrical products from brands, including switchgear, circuit breakers, panelboards, fuses, wiring, lighting, conduit, tools, and safety gear. As an official Siemens distributor, it offers wholesale pricing and operates a warehouse with fast shipping and local pickup options. Beyond product supply, Castillo Electric Distribution provides consulting services such as project consultation, material sourcing, logistics support, and product guidance. It also runs a recurring supplies program for consistent material delivery and collaborates with Mario Castillo Electric for installation and electrical contracting services, delivering a full-service approach from product selection to project execution.

Castillo Electric Distribution serves electricians, contractors, facility managers, property managers, and business owners across residential, commercial, and industrial projects. Its customer base includes professionals working on new builds, service upgrades, temporary power setups, and retrofit jobs. The company emphasizes trade-driven expertise, with staff who have hands-on field experience to ensure accurate recommendations.

The company differentiates itself through its electrician-run ownership, transparent pricing, and a loyalty program called Castillo EDGE that offers discounts, flexible fulfillment, and volume-order terms. Its core values—customer first, integrity, trade-driven expertise, value-driven pricing, and operational excellence—guide its focus on keeping projects on schedule and budgets intact.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale electrical distribution", "Electrical product consulting", "Project consultation", "Material sourcing", "Logistics support", "Recurring supply programs", "Switchgear and component supply", "Lighting and control systems supply", "Wiring and conduit supply", "Tools and safety gear supply", "Installation support via partner", "Troubleshooting and maintenance advice"], "industries": ["Residential electrical", "Commercial construction", "Industrial construction", "Electrical contracting", "Facility management", "Property management"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Official Siemens Distributor", "Electrician-run business with trade-driven expertise", "Castillo EDGE loyalty program with discounts and flexible terms", "Fast shipping and local pickup nationwide", "Consulting services including project consultation and material sourcing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 -> db", "Headquarters in Signal Hill, California -> db", "Official Siemens Distributor -> /", "Wholesale electrical supplier -> /", "Electrician-run business -> /", "Offers consulting services -> /, /about-us, /services", "Collaborates with Mario Castillo Electric for installation and electrical contracting services -> /, /about-us, /services", "Serves residential, commercial, and industrial projects -> /about-us", "Offers recurring supplies service -> /services", "Provides project consultation, material sourcing, logistics support, product guidance -> /services", "Loyalty program: Castillo EDGE -> /", "Fast shipping and local pickup -> /services", "Products: switchgear, circuit breakers, panelboards, fuses, wiring, lighting, conduit, tools, safety gear -> /about-us, /services", "Core values: Customer First, Integrity & Accountability, Trade-Driven Expertise, Value-Driven, Operational Excellence -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Official Siemens Distributor", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='castillo-electric-distribution' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1979, Cave Creek Welding has operated from its Cave Creek, Arizona location for over four decades. The family-owned business began as a custom metalwork shop serving the local community.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication and welding for both residential and construction-phase projects. Its capabilities include structural steel fabrication, fire pits, fireplace screens, gates, hand rails, and fences, with in-house powder coating and installation services. The team manages projects from concept through completion, handling design, fabrication, and on-site installation.

The company serves property owners, architects, and structural engineers across Arizona, delivering custom metalwork for residential homes, commercial spaces, and architectural installations. Projects range from decorative gates and handrails to structural steel components.

Cave Creek Welding differentiates itself through clear communication, on-time delivery, and close collaboration with design professionals. A client testimonial describes the firm as a real family business offering great workmanship and value, highlighting its reputation for reliability and craftsmanship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding (residential and construction-phase)", "Structural steel fabrication", "Fire pit fabrication", "Fireplace screen fabrication", "Gate fabrication", "Hand rail fabrication", "Fence fabrication", "Powder coating", "Installation services"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Clear communication, on-time delivery, and flawless results on every project", "Close collaboration with property owners, architects, and structural engineers", "Family-owned business valued for workmanship and value", "Full project management from concept to completion"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us (testimonial)", "Location Cave Creek, AZ -> /", "Products: Structural Steel, Fire Pits, Fireplace Screens, Gates, Hand Rails, Fences -> /", "Services: custom metalwork, welding, fabrication, installation -> description", "Collaborates with property owners, architects, structural engineers -> description", "Clear communication, on-time delivery, flawless results -> description", "Powder coating mentioned -> /about-us (testimonial)"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Specializing in both residential and construction-phase welding, we are known for building extraordinary, one-of-a-kind structures that combine form, function, and unmatched craftsmanship.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cave-creek-welding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cavecloth operates from Springdale, Arkansas, in the Ozarks region. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed, nor are its founders named in available sources. The brand positions itself as a local apparel label with the tagline "Made In the Ozarks."

The company designs and sells printed garments, primarily short- and long-sleeve T-shirts featuring Arkansas-centric graphics such as the "WU Pig," "Call It," "Woo Graphic," "Arkansas Home," and "Buffalo National River" designs. Cavecloth states it uses eco-friendly, soft inks for printing, emphasizing that the ink does not crack or peel and breathes with the fabric. No facility size, headcount, or production volumes are provided.

Cavecloth sells directly to consumers through its e-commerce website, offering free shipping on U.S. orders over $75. The product lineup includes multiple collections—Ozark, Arkansas, and Spring/Summer—with individual shirts priced around $25 to $30. No industrial or wholesale customer base is described in the source material.

The company highlights its ink formulation as a key differentiator: eco-friendly, crack- and peel-resistant, and breathable to avoid "sweaty spots in the summertime." The origin story or specific mission behind the brand is not detailed in the available information.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Apparel printing with eco-friendly inks"], "industries": ["Apparel retail", "Consumer goods"], "materials": ["Eco-friendly inks", "Cloth"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Eco-friendly, soft inks that do not crack or peel", "Inks breathe with the fabric to reduce sweaty spots", "Apparel printed and marketed as \"Made In the Ozarks\"", "Free shipping on U.S. orders over $75"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Springdale, Arkansas -> db", "Sells printed apparel with Arkansas/Ozarks themes -> /", "Uses eco-friendly, soft inks that do not crack or peel -> /", "Inks breathe with fabric to avoid sweaty spots -> /", "Markets products as ''Made In the Ozarks'' -> /", "Offers free shipping on U.S. orders over $75 -> /", "Product prices range $25-$30 -> /", "Collections: Ozark, Arkansas, Spring/Summer -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We only use eco-friendly, soft inks to print our products.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cavecloth' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cedar Creek Energy operates from Blaine, Minnesota, where it was founded in 2007 as an electrical and general contractor specializing in solar energy. The company began with a focus on solar development, engineering-procurement-construction (EPC) services, and ongoing operations and maintenance, offering all three disciplines under a single organization.

The firm designs, installs, and operates commercial photovoltaic arrays across the Midwest, integrating energy storage systems where required. Its scope covers full EPC delivery — from initial engineering and procurement through construction and commissioning — as well as long-term O&M support. To date, the company has completed thousands of solar projects of varying size and complexity.

Primary customers are commercial and industrial property owners seeking to reduce operating expenses and hedge against rising utility rates. Cedar Creek Energy also assists clients with financing structures, incentive applications, and rebate programs, including Minnesota''s Property Assessed Clean Energy (PACE) financing. The company has executed the first approved MnPACE-financed solar project in the state.

The integrated development-EPC-O&M model is cited as a key differentiator, allowing the team to manage the full solar asset lifecycle without handoffs between separate vendors. Leadership emphasizes transparent consulting, illustrated by instances where the company advised against installations that would not meet a client''s energy-offset goals.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Solar PV installation", "Engineering, Procurement, and Construction (EPC)", "Operations and Maintenance (O&M)", "Energy storage system integration", "Commercial solar project development", "Financing and incentive consulting", "MnPACE financing facilitation"], "industries": ["Commercial real estate", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated development, EPC, and O&M under one roof", "Thousands of commercial solar projects completed across the Midwest", "Assistance with financing, incentives, and rebate programs including MnPACE", "Energy storage integration with solar PV arrays", "Transparent consulting that may recommend against uneconomical installations"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 -> db", "Headquarters Blaine, Minnesota -> db", "Electrical and general contractor, solar development, EPC, O&M -> db", "Designs, installs, operates commercial solar PV arrays in Midwest -> db", "Thousands of projects completed -> db", "Services: commercial solar panels, EPC, energy storage -> /", "Assists with financing, rebates, incentives, MnPACE -> /", "First approved MnPACE-financed project -> /", "Awards: MNSEIA 2024 Project of the Year, 2025 Top Solar Contractor, Star Tribune Minnesota''s Best -> /about-us", "Integrated development-EPC-O&M model -> db", "Transparent consulting, may advise against uneconomical installs -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Cedar Creek Energy is an electrical and general contractor with a specific focus on solar development, EPC services, maximizing system operation, and system maintenance.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cedar-creek-energy-solar-company-minnesota' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Celestica operates a state-of-the-art facility in Maple Grove, Minnesota, focused on aerospace, defense, and health technology markets. The site joined Celestica''s global network as a newer addition and was formerly known as AbelConn, LLC, which remains the legal entity. No founding year is disclosed for the Maple Grove operation.

The Maple Grove site combines an in-house engineering center of excellence with on-site manufacturing, providing build-to-print production, electromechanical assembly, and obsolescence management. Capabilities span RF and systems engineering, design for manufacturing and test, prototype delivery in four to six weeks, and volume production of printed circuit card assemblies, chassis, line-replaceable units, and backplanes under ITAR compliance. The facility also serves as a center of excellence for product licensing, repair, and overhaul services, offering automated soldering, plating, conformal coating, and RFID-enabled smart shelving.

Celestica Maple Grove serves commercial aerospace and defense primes, supplying high-reliability systems and sub-systems found on most commercial aircraft in service today, as well as defense programs operating in harsh land, sea, air, and space environments. In health technology, the site partners with early-stage innovators and multinational medical device companies to produce finished medical devices, leveraging regulatory expertise and supply chain resilience.

The company emphasizes accelerated time-to-market and quality through co-located engineering and manufacturing, predictive supply chain analytics, and a full-lifecycle approach from design through after-market support. Its differentiators include rapid prototyping, ITAR-compliant volume production, and integrated repair and overhaul capabilities.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','ROHS','AS9100','NADCAP','ISO13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering Services", "RF Engineering", "Systems Engineering", "BOM Analysis (RoHS, REACH, WEEE, Obsolescence)", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM) and Design for Testability (DFT)", "Test Development Strategy", "Product Testing and Certification", "Component Obsolescence and Production Continuity", "CCA Manufacturing", "Chassis and LRU Manufacturing", "Backplane Manufacturing", "ITAR-Compliant Volume Production", "Electronics Assembly", "Inspection and Test", "Automated Soldering", "Plating", "Conformal Coating", "Licensing and Repair & Overhaul (R&O)", "Smart Shelving", "RFID Tracking", "Prototyping", "Supply Chain Strategy", "Industrialization", "Process Qualification (Control Plans, PFMEA, Gage R&R)", "Design for Supply Chain (DfSC)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Commercial Aerospace", "HealthTech", "Medical Devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Automated soldering systems", "Plating lines", "Conformal coating systems", "Smart shelving", "RFID tracking systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Prototypes in 4-6 weeks (+ Material Lead Times)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Prototypes delivered in 4\u20136 weeks (plus material lead times)", "ITAR-compliant volume production", "Co-located engineering center of excellence and manufacturing", "Center of excellence for product licensing, repair, and overhaul", "Predictive supply chain risk management with analytics"], "facts_used": ["Maple Grove, Minnesota location -> /", "Formerly AbelConn, LLC -> /", "Engineering center of excellence co-located with manufacturing -> /", "Build-to-print manufacturing, electromechanical product support, obsolescence management -> /", "Center of excellence for product licensing, repair and overhaul services -> /", "Certifications: ITAR, RoHS, AS9100, NADCAP, ISO13485 -> db", "Prototypes in 4-6 weeks -> /", "ITAR-compliant volume production -> /", "Serves commercial aerospace and defense primes -> /", "Partners with medical device companies -> /", "Capabilities: RF engineering, systems engineering, BOM analysis, DFM/DFT, test development, product testing, component obsolescence, CCA/chassis/LRU/backplane manufacturing, electronics assembly, inspection, automated soldering, plating, conformal coating, licensing/R&O, smart shelving, RFID tracking -> /", "Industries: Aerospace, Defense, Commercial Aerospace, HealthTech, Medical Devices -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our state-of-the-art facility features an in-house engineering center of excellence, enabling innovative turn-key product development solutions. The Maple Grove operation also hosts on-site manufacturing, offering a broad range of services including build-to-print manufacturing, electromechanical product support and obsolescence management.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='celestica' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Centek Molding Co. LLC operates from Buena Park, California. The company has accumulated over 35 years of experience in plastic injection molding, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The shop provides custom plastic injection molding services, including process development, mold testing, and qualification (IQ, OQ, PQ, DOE) using Decoupled Molding II techniques. Its press fleet spans 35 to 200 tons of clamping pressure with shot capacities from 0.13 to 13.10 ounces, supporting both low- and high-volume runs without a minimum order requirement. Additional capabilities cover rapid prototyping, insert and over molding, and mold construction or repair for hot-runner, cold-runner, core-pull, unscrew, and valve-gate systems.

Centek serves customers across medical, industrial, construction, automotive, irrigation, electrical, household, and sports sectors. The company works with commodity, engineering, and specialty-grade plastics in any color.

