UPDATE companies SET description='Central Cable Contractors Inc is based in Waupun, Wisconsin, and was founded in 1974. The company began as a cable plowing operation with a handful of employees and has grown to over 185 staff.

The firm provides underground construction services for telecommunications infrastructure. Its core processes include cable plowing, directional boring, fiber optic cable jetting, trenching, splicing, cable locating, drop installation, and hydro excavation. The fleet comprises more than 35 cable plows (up to 60,000-pound Caterpillar track machines), 50 directional boring machines (including rock-boring units), over 75 trenching units, 25 large hydro excavation trucks, and 12 mini trailer vacuum systems. Crews are each equipped with cable jetting systems. Project scale ranges from single-day drops to installations exceeding 300 miles of plowing and bores over 1,500 feet.

Primary customers are telecommunications providers, broadband cooperatives, and contractors building fiber-to-the-home networks. Documented projects include a 48-mile fiber network for South Slope Cooperative Communications in Iowa and an 89-mile rural FTTH build for CTC Technology connecting 270 homes. The company also references work for Comm 1 and other community broadband initiatives.

Central Cable states its mission is to lead in quality and production while keeping customer relationships as the top priority. It emphasizes a safe, family-oriented work environment and long-term employee retention, noting that many cable locators have 15-plus years of experience. The company says it stays committed to relationships with customers and employees as the foundation for continued prosperity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable plowing", "Directional boring", "Fiber optic cable jetting", "Trenching (backhoe, excavator, mini excavator, chain trencher)", "Splicing (copper, loose tube, ribbon, microfiber, FTTH architectures)", "Cable locating", "Drop installation", "Hydro excavation", "OTDR testing at multiple wavelengths", "Hot cuts and emergency restoration", "Pre-connectorized plant design", "Open architecture pedestal construction"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Broadband", "Fiber optic networks", "Fiber-to-the-home (FTTH)", "Rural broadband", "Cooperative communications"], "materials": ["Fiber optic cable (loose tube, ribbon, microfiber)", "Copper cable", "Conduit systems"], "equipment": ["Caterpillar 60,000-lb track cable plow", "Directional boring machines (50 units, various sizes)", "Rock boring equipment (two sets)", "Trenching equipment: backhoes, excavators, mini excavators, chain trenchers (75+ units)", "Hydro excavation trucks (25+ large units)", "Mini trailer vacuum systems (12 units)", "Cable jetting systems (one per crew)"], "volume": "Projects from single-day drops to 300+ mile plowing installations; bores exceeding 1,500 feet", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fleet of 35+ cable plows including 60,000-lb Caterpillar track machines", "50 directional boring machines with rock-boring capability", "75+ trenching units matched to site conditions", "25+ hydro excavation trucks and 12 mini trailer vac systems for tight easements", "Each crew equipped with independent cable jetting system",