UPDATE companies SET description='Central Coast Live Foods operates from Watsonville, California, and traces its roots to 2014 when Central Coast Juicery opened its first location in Pacific Grove. The business was built around a mission to bring fresh, organic juice to the local community; a founder named Max is referenced in customer feedback discussing order fulfillment. What began as a juice shop evolved after customers repeatedly asked for more food options, the team to develop a single product that met their ingredient standards.

The company manufactures Kraut Krackers, a fermented cracker made from just four organic ingredients. The production process centers on fermentation, which the company says enhances nutrient absorption and provides probiotics, dietary fiber, electrolytes, and healthy fats. The crackers are soy-free, sugar-free, seed-oil-free, gluten-free, and vegan. From a kitchen that could not keep up with demand, production scaled to the point that the product now sits on retail shelves across California, serving hundreds of direct customers.

The primary buyers are health-focused consumers seeking gut-health support, including people with conditions such as Crohn''s disease, as well as vegan and fitness-oriented shoppers looking for a post-workout snack with electrolytes. The product is positioned in the organic snack, functional food, and gut-health categories, sold both direct-to-consumer and through California retail accounts.

The founders say they created Kraut Krackers because it was the only food product that matched their criteria for nutrient-dense, minimally processed ingredients without ultra-processed additives. Customer demand outpaced their ability to make the crackers by hand, prompting them to ramp up production and expand distribution.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fermentation", "Organic snack food manufacturing", "Clean-label product formulation", "Retail distribution across California", "Direct-to-consumer e-commerce fulfillment"], "industries": ["Organic food manufacturing", "Healthy snack foods", "Functional food and gut health products", "Vegan food products", "Sports nutrition snacks"], "materials": ["Organic vegetables", "Fermented vegetable ingredients", "Dietary fiber", "Probiotics", "Electrolytes", "Healthy fats"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Just 4 organic, simple ingredients", "Fermentation for probiotic and nutrient absorption benefits", "Free of soy, sugar, seed oils, and gluten", "Vegan formulation designed not to taste like cardboard", "Free U.S. shipping on orders over $105"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 -> db", "First location in Pacific Grove, CA -> /", "Headquarters in Watsonville, California -> db", "Founder referenced as Max in customer review -> /", "Product: Kraut Krackers, fermented crackers with 4 organic ingredients -> /", "Process: fermentation enhances nutrient absorption, provides probiotics, fiber, electrolytes, healthy fats -> /", "Attributes: soy-free, sugar-free, seed-oil-free, gluten-free, vegan -> /", "Scale: retail stores across California, hundreds of customers -> /", "Target customers: gut-health seekers, Crohn''s sufferers, vegans, fitness enthusiasts -> /", "Origin story: created because product met standards for nutrient-dense, minimally processed food -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We decided to ramp up the production and now Kraut Krackers are in retail stores all across California.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='central-coast-live-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Central Custom Molding was founded in 1968 in Cheyenne, Wyoming, as a family-owned injection molding operation. The company''s homepage notes that "our family has been manufacturing in the US since 1968," and the facility is deliberately positioned in the center of the country to mitigate risks from hurricanes, earthquakes, and political unrest.

The shop runs plastic injection molding on machines ranging from 7 to 460 tons, supporting mold design and manufacturing from proof-of-concept tools to multi-cavity high-production molds. It also operates a Class 7 cleanroom for medical components and provides assembly, packaging, and third-party logistics services. The company offers part design, design for manufacturing, and part engineering as part of its full-service model.

Customers span medical device manufacturers requiring cleanroom molding, aerospace and defense programs (including components on James Cameron''s deep-sea submersible, corporate jets, and autonomous aircraft), water filtration systems for developing regions, and sporting goods producers.

