UPDATE companies SET description='Click Therapeutics was founded in 2012 in New York City by David Benshoof Klein, who recognized the profound influence of smartphones on behavior and cognition. Klein coined the term "Digital Therapeutics™" and established the company to develop, validate, and commercialize software as prescription medical treatments for patients with unmet medical needs. The venture-backed firm counts HIG, Accelmed, and Sanofi Ventures among its investors.

The company operates a multimodal, AI-enabled platform that combines neuroscience with proprietary neuromodulatory mechanisms to create prescription digital therapeutics (PDTs) and Software-Enhanced Drugs™. Its pipeline includes CT-152 (Rejoyn™), an FDA-cleared adjunctive treatment for major depressive disorder developed with Otsuka; CT-155 (Motivista) for negative symptoms of schizophrenia; AspyreRx™ for type 2 diabetes; and CT-132 for episodic migraine, all of which have received FDA authorization. Additional candidates target opioid use disorder, multiple sclerosis, atopic dermatitis, obesity, oncology, insomnia, and acute coronary syndrome. A multidisciplinary team of clinicians, researchers, and technologists drives development from discovery through pivotal trials.

Click Therapeutics serves patients, prescribing physicians, and biopharma partners across the digital therapeutics, software-as-a-medical-device, and life-sciences sectors. Its treatments are regulated by the FDA and global authorities as medical devices and are prescribed and reimbursed as drug-software combination products.

The company''s stated mission is to provide global access to safe and effective prescription digital therapeutics. Its differentiators include a platform-based approach that integrates clinically proven therapies with software-driven neuromodulation, a track record of first-of-kind FDA clearances, and a commitment to rigorous clinical validation through randomized controlled trials.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Prescription digital therapeutic development", "Clinical trial design and execution (Phase 1\u20133)", "FDA regulatory submission and clearance (510(k), De Novo)", "Software as a Medical Device (SaMD) development", "Digital therapeutic platform development", "Neuromodulatory mechanism research", "AI-enabled digital therapeutic development", "Software-Enhanced Drug\u2122 development", "Patient-centric digital treatment design", "Real-world evidence generation", "Peer-reviewed publication", "Pharmaceutical partner collaboration"], "industries": ["Prescription Digital Therapeutics", "Digital Therapeutics", "Software as a Medical Device (SaMD)", "Biotechnology", "Pharmaceuticals", "Healthcare", "Life Sciences", "Medical Devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First FDA-cleared prescription app for adjunctive MDD treatment (developed with Otsuka)", "AI-enabled prescription digital therapeutics platform", "Multimodal platform combining neuroscience with proprietary neuromodulatory mechanisms", "Software-Enhanced Drugs\u2122 combining software with pharmacotherapy", "Clinical validation through randomized controlled trials across multiple indications"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 in New York City by David Benshoof Klein -> /about", "Coined term Digital Therapeutics\u2122 -> /about", "Develops, validates, commercializes software as prescription medical treatments -> /about, db description", "Venture-backed by HIG, Accelmed, Sanofi Ventures -> /about", "AI-enabled prescription digital therapeutics platform -> /about", "Multimodal platform combining neuroscience with proprietary neuromodulatory mechanisms -> /", "Software-Enhanced Drugs\u2122 combining software with pharmacotherapy -> /", "CT-152 (Rejoyn\u2122) FDA-cleared for MDD adjunctive treatment with Otsuka -> /about", "CT-155 (Motivista) FDA authorized for schizophrenia negative symptoms -> /about", "AspyreRx\u2122 FDA authorized for type 2 diabetes -> /about", "CT-132 FDA authorized for episodic migraine -> /about", "Pipeline candidates for OUD, MS, atopic dermatitis, obesity, oncology, insomnia, acute coronary syndrome -> /about", "Multidisciplinary team of clinicians, researchers, technologists -> /about", "Regulated by FDA and globally as medical devices -> /, industries_served", "Prescribed and reimbursed as drug-software combination products -> db products", "Mission: provide global access to safe and effective prescription digital therapeutics -> /about", "ISO13485 certification -> db certifications", "Awards: PharmaVoice 100, Builtin Best Places to Work, DHNY Hall of Fame, Deloitte Technology Fast 500 -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db linkedin_url"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We develop, validate, and commercialize software as prescription medical treatments for people with unmet medical needs.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pharmavoice/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='click-therapeutics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ClickFold Plastics was founded in 2001 in Charlotte, North Carolina, to address a gap in the market for custom plastic enclosures and parts in smaller volumes. The company developed a zero-tooling fabrication process that eliminates the need for expensive molds, targeting industrial buyers who previously had to choose between off-the-shelf enclosures, costly injection molding, or sheet metal fabrication.

The company produces custom plastic housings, enclosures, covers, panels, and similar components using CNC machining, 3D printing, digital graphics, UV printing, EMI shielding, assembly, and packaging services. Its facility straddles the North Carolina–South Carolina border near Charlotte Douglas International Airport, operates multiple shifts in an air-conditioned, smoke-free environment, and focuses on just-in-time delivery for low-volume production runs.

ClickFold serves OEMs across industrial controls, medical devices, communications, gaming and simulators, building controls, measuring equipment, government and military, and commercial vehicles. Customers receive virtual 3D prototypes for review before physical first articles are produced using the same materials and processes as final production.

The zero-tooling approach allows cost-effective low-volume manufacturing with no minimum order quantities and a typical concept-to-production timeline of under four weeks. The quality system has been ISO 9001 certified since 2017, and the company maintains international production-transfer partnerships with firms in Germany and Brazil, as well as collaborations with local universities.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining", "3D printing", "Digital graphics printing", "UV printing", "EMI shielding", "Assembly", "Packaging", "Custom kitting", "Virtual prototyping", "Rapid prototyping", "Metal substitution", "CAD design", "Reverse engineering", "Material sourcing", "Zero-tooling fabrication", "Just-in-time manufacturing"], "industries": ["Industrial Controls", "Medical Devices", "Communications", "Gaming/Simulators", "Building Controls", "Measuring Equipment", "Government/Military", "Commercial Vehicles"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low-volume production runs", "lead_time": "Under 4 weeks from concept to production", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-tooling process eliminates mold costs", "No minimum order quantities", "Concept to production in under four weeks", "ISO 9001 certified quality management", "International production transfer via partner network"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Charlotte, NC -> /about-us", "Zero-tooling process -> /", "ISO 9001 certified since 2017 -> /about-us", "Industries served: Industrial Controls, Medical Devices, Communications, Gaming/Simulators, Building Controls, Measuring Equipment, Government/Military, Commercial Vehicles -> /", "Capabilities: CNC machining, 3D printing, digital graphics, UV printing, EMI shielding, assembly, packaging -> /about-us", "No minimum order quantities -> /", "Concept to production under 4 weeks -> /", "Facility on NC/SC state line near Charlotte airport -> /about-us", "Partnerships with CubiDesign (Germa