UPDATE companies SET description='Colorado Microcircuits (CMI) operates a custom-built facility in Loveland, Colorado, specializing in highly automated contract assembly of microwave and RF semiconductors.

CMI assembles single and multi-die components using off-the-shelf or custom packages, including ceramic, air cavity lead frames, overmold lead frames, and high-performance laminates. Its processes cover die attach, wire bonding (short, tuned, and stacked wires), soldering, mixed assembly of ICs and surface-mount components, GGI flip chip, and stacked die. The facility runs industry-standard automated semiconductor assembly equipment and produces volumes ranging from thousands to millions of units per year, with documented ISO 9001 procedures yielding high quality and extremely high yield rates.

The company serves the RF and microwave semiconductor market, acting as a key assembly partner for industry leaders in that sector. Customers include commercial-volume buyers seeking an onshore U.S. partner for competitive pricing and reduced geopolitical supply-chain risk; CMI emphasizes turnkey solutions and short production lead times for clients located within a few hours'' drive of its Colorado plant.

CMI differentiates itself through its niche in innovative air cavity packaging and its fully automated, ISO 9001-documented process that extends to each new product. The firm highlights its ability to mitigate supply-chain risk as a high-volume onshore supplier, and its mixed-assembly capability that places surface-mount passives inside air-cavity packages.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automated IC assembly", "Die attach", "Wire bonding (short, tuned, stacked)", "Soldering", "Mixed assembly (ICs and surface-mount components)", "Flip chip (GGI)", "Stacked die assembly", "High thermal conductivity epoxy attach", "Air cavity packaging (ceramic, lead frame, overmold, laminate)", "QFN packaging (plastic, co-fired ceramic, laminate, overmold)", "Turnkey assembly solutions"], "industries": ["Microwave semiconductors", "RF semiconductors", "RF and microwave market"], "materials": ["Ceramic", "Air cavity lead frames", "Overmold lead frames", "High-performance laminates", "Surface mount passives", "High thermal conductivity epoxies"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Thousands to millions of units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully automated IC assembly process documented to ISO 9001", "Innovative air cavity packaging (ceramic, lead frame, overmold, laminate)", "Production volumes from thousands to millions of units", "Turnkey solutions with short lead times for U.S. customers", "Onshore manufacturing mitigating geopolitical supply chain risk"], "facts_used": ["Location: Loveland, CO -> db", "Specialty: highly automated contract assembly of microwave and RF semiconductors -> /about-us", "Volumes: thousands to millions -> /about-us", "Packages: ceramic, air cavity lead frames, overmold lead frames, high-performance laminates -> /about-us", "Processes: die attach, wire bonding, soldering, mixed assembly, flip chip, stacked die -> /about-us", "Facility: custom-built, industry-standard automated semiconductor assembly equipment -> /about-us", "Certification: ISO 9001 compliant -> /about-us and db", "Differentiator: innovative air cavity packaging -> /about-us", "Onshore US-based manufacturing mitigates geopolitical supply chain risks -> /about-us", "Turnkey solutions with short production lead times -> /about-us", "QFN packages offered (plastic, co-fired ceramic, laminate, overmold) -> /", "Automation of every step of IC assembly -> /", "High yield rates from documented process -> /", "Mixed assembly process combining soldering with die attach and wire bonding -> /", "GGI flip chip recently added -> /about-us", "High thermal conductivity epoxies -> /about-us", "Short/tuned/stacked wires -> /about-us", "Stacked die -> /about-us", "Off-the-shelf and custom packages -> /about-us", "Located within a few hours of any US customer -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Colorado Microcircuits'' primary specialty is highly automated contract assembly of microwave and RF semiconductors in the United States", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='colorado-microcircuits' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Colorado Mountain Solar operates from Buena Vista, Colorado, delivering solar energy solutions to customers across the region. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founder names.

The firm designs and installs both grid-tied and off-grid solar arrays for residential and commercial properties, incorporating battery storage and backup generators where needed. Its services extend to system upgrades, diagnostics and repair, preventive maintenance, performance optimization, priority response, and pre-purchase inspections that produce a detailed Solar System Health Report. Each project begins with an evaluation of energy usage, site conditions, and long-term objectives to tailor the system design.

