UPDATE companies SET description='Colorado Threads was founded in 2014 in Lakewood, Colorado, with a mission to keep plastic out of landfills and oceans. The company operates a boutique manufacturing facility and design studio in nearby Denver, where it produces its activewear line.

The company manufactures activewear including yoga pants, tanks, hats, joggers, and accessories. Production is hand-crafted at the Denver facility using recycled polyester derived from plastic bottles; fabric waste is recycled into headbands and garments are upcycled. The brand distributes its products across 23 countries.

Colorado Threads serves the activewear, yoga apparel, and outdoor recreation markets. Its customer base includes wellness-focused consumers and outdoor enthusiasts. Concrete product examples include the Red Rocks concert yoga pants and the Grassroots x Colorado Threads Cosmic Wolf collaboration line.

The company differentiates itself through its Certified B Corporation status, which recognizes three impact business models: local economic impact through Denver-based production and regional sourcing within a 1,500-mile radius; sustainable practices such as BPA-free recycled materials and zero-waste manufacturing; and community giving that directs a portion of revenue to local nonprofits and youth programs.', certifications=ARRAY['B Corp Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut and sew apparel manufacturing", "Product design and development", "Textile recycling and upcycling", "Local supply chain management"], "industries": ["Activewear", "Yoga apparel", "Sportswear", "Outdoor apparel"], "materials": ["Recycled polyester (from plastic bottles)", "Recycled fibers", "BPA-free fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified B Corporation with three Impact Business Models", "Local manufacturing at boutique facility in Denver", "Activewear made from recycled plastic bottles", "Zero-waste production recycling scrap into accessories", "Revenue share with local nonprofits and youth programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 -> db", "Headquarters Lakewood, Colorado -> db", "Boutique manufacturing facility in Denver -> /", "Certified B Corporation -> /", "Products made from recycled water bottles -> /", "Zero-waste initiatives (recycling waste into headbands, upcycling) -> /", "Community giving to local nonprofits -> /", "Operates in 23 countries -> /", "Product examples: Red Rocks yoga pants, Grassroots collaboration -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a Colorado Activewear Brand that Make Hand Crafted Active Wear for the Enthusiastic Wanderer at our Boutique Manufacturing Facility and Design Studio in Denver, Colorado.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links