UPDATE companies SET description='Columbus Machine Works was founded in 1997 in Columbus, Ohio, by Mike Stacey, who began as a job-shop machinist commuting by bicycle to serve local customers. The company has grown into a full-service machine shop operating from a facility on Fairwood Avenue.

The shop provides CNC milling and turning, wire EDM, conventional machining, repair and retrofit services, and welding and fabrication. The facility spans two buildings with bridge cranes, forklifts, and a dedicated inspection room.

The company serves the medical equipment industry and other industrial clients in Central Ohio, producing OEM replacement parts, prototypes, jigs, fixtures, and tooling. It also offers on-site evaluation, reverse engineering, inventory stocking, and 24/7 emergency breakdown service.

