UPDATE companies SET description='Consolidated Metco Inc., doing business as ConMet, was founded in 1964 in Clackamas, Oregon, as part of Portland Freightliner, a subsidiary of Consolidated Freightways. The company became independent in 1987 before being acquired by Varlen Corp. in 1989 and later by Amsted Industries in 1999. Today it operates as a subsidiary of Amsted Industries, with its corporate headquarters in Vancouver, Washington, and a major manufacturing campus in Clackamas.

ConMet designs and manufactures wheel-end systems, structural plastic components, permanent-mold aluminum castings, and aerodynamic devices for commercial vehicles. Its processes include aluminum die casting, permanent-mold casting, CNC machining, plastic injection molding and assembly, and wheel-end foundry and machining. The company runs 13 to 16 global manufacturing locations across North America, China, and Europe, encompassing foundries, machine shops, assembly lines, and a technical center. Annual output exceeds 3 billion products, with more than 60 million hubs produced and 18 million vehicles on the road equipped with ConMet parts.

The company serves original equipment manufacturers and commercial fleets in the heavy-duty truck and trailer market, as well as the North American aftermarket. Recent customer examples include European OEMs accessing ConMet''s wheel-end engineering and production at IAA, and fleets purchasing TruCast brake drums through the aftermarket network. ConMet also supports electrification initiatives through its eMobility solutions.

ConMet emphasizes collaborative design–development–testing–validation cycles, advanced automation, and sustainable manufacturing practices such as high-efficiency furnaces, heat-treat optimization, and extensive recycling. The company states its purpose is a "relentless pursuit to imagine and engineer transformative solutions that improve the success of our customers and the lives of our employees."', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum die casting", "Permanent-mold aluminum casting", "CNC machining", "Plastic injection molding and assembly", "Wheel-end foundry and machining", "Structural plastic component manufacturing", "Wheel-end assembly and testing", "Aftermarket fulfillment and distribution", "Technical training and certification programs", "Aerodynamic device manufacturing (TruckWings)", "eMobility system integration"], "industries": ["Commercial vehicle", "Heavy-duty truck and trailer", "Aftermarket parts", "Electrification/eMobility"], "materials": ["Aluminum alloys", "Structural plastics", "Iron (foundry)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["60+ years of wheel-end experience with 60+ million hubs produced", "Full-service metal casting provider for commercial vehicle components", "TruckWings automatic cab-trailer aerodynamic device", "13 global manufacturing locations with advanced automation and quality systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1964 as Consolidated Metco Inc. part of Portland Freightliner -> /about", "Corporate headquarters in Vancouver, Washington -> / (homepage)", "Clackamas, Oregon facility for aluminum die cast solutions -> / (homepage)", "13 global manufacturing locations across North America, China, Europe -> / (homepage)", "60+ million hubs produced, 3 billion+ products shipped annually, 18 million+ vehicles on road -> / (homepage)", "Acquired by Amsted Industries in 1999 -> /about", "Products: wheel ends, structural plastics, aluminum castings, TruckWings, eMob